  "original_lyrics": "[intro]\n- - - + -\nAnthony works in the grocery store\nSavin' his pennies for someday\nMama Leone left note on the door,\nShe said, \"Sonny, move out to the country.\"\nWorkin' too hard can give you\nheart attack-ack-ack-ack-ack\nYou oughta know by now (You oughta know by now)\nWho needs house out in Hackensack?\nIs that what you get for your money?\nIt seems such waste of time\nIf that's what it's all about\nIf that's movin' up then I'm movin' out.\nSergeant O'Leary is walkin' the beat\nAt night he becomes bartender\nHe works at Mister Cacciatore's down on Sullivan Street\nAcross from the medical center\nHe's tradin' in his Chevy for Cadillac\nYou oughta know by now (You oughta know by now)\nAnd if he can't drive with broken back\nAt least he can polish the fenders\nIt seems such waste of time\nIf that's what it's all about\nIf that's movin' up then I'm movin' out.\nYou should never argue with crazy mi-mi-mi-mi-mind\nYou oughta know by now\nYou can pay Uncle Sam with overtime\nIs that all you get for your money?\nIf that's what you have in mind\nIf that's what you're all about\nGood luck movin' up cos I'm movin' out.",
